 the retrieval of solutes from the xylem sap.\")\n4505:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000074 obo:PO_0000066)\n4506:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000074 \"obsolete epithem cell\")\n4507:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000074 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n4509:# Class: obo:CL_0000075 (columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell)\n4511:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO:0002065\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000075 \"A columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell is a cell usually found in a two dimensional sheet with a free surface. Columnar/cuboidal epithelial cells take on the shape of a column or cube.\")\n4512:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000075 \"columnar/cuboidal epithelial cell\")\n4513:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000075 obo:CL_0000066)\n4515:# Class: obo:CL_0000076 (squamous epithelial cell)\n4517:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000076 \"CALOHA:TS-1249\")\n4518:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000076 \"squamous epithelial cell\")\n4519:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000076 obo:CL_0000066)\n4521:# Class: obo:CL_0000077 (mesothelial cell)\n4523:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000077 \"A flat, squamous-like epithelial cell of mesodermal origin. It forms the mesothelium, which lines the body's serous cavities including the pleural, peritoneal, and pericardial spaces. This cell plays a crucial role in synthesizing and secreting lubricants, such as glycosaminoglycans and surfactants, which minimize friction between adjacent tissues during movement.\")\n4524:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000077 \"FMA:66773\")\n4525:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000077 \"mesotheliocyte\")\n4526:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26106328\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000077 \"Mesothelial cells, which morphologically resemble squamous epithelial cells, express both epithelial markers (cytokeratins) and mesenchymal markers (vimentin), reflecting their mesodermal origin. They feature surface microvilli and apical-basal polarity. Under certain conditions, they can undergo mesothelial-to-mesenchymal transition. These cells also produce extracellular matrix proteins, maintain serosal homeostasis, and facilitate fluid transport.\")\n4527:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000077 \"mesothelial cell\")\n4528:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 obo:CL_0000076)\n4529:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001136))\n4530:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000077 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000222))\n4532:# Class: obo:CL_0000078 (peridermal cell)\n4534:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000078 \"peridermal cell\")\n4535:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000078 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000076 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003055)))\n4537:# Class: obo:CL_0000079 (stratified epithelial cell)\n4539:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1016/B978-0-12-410424-2.00003-2\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.biologyonline.com/dictionary/stratified-epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000079 \"An epithelial cell, organized into multiple layers, with only the basal layer being in contact with the basement membrane.\")\n4540:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000079 \"stratified epithelial cell\")\n4541:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000079 obo:CL_0000066)\n4542:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000357))\n4544:# Class: obo:CL_0000080 (circulating cell)\n4546:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000080 \"A cell which moves among different tissues of the body, via blood, lymph, or other medium.\")\n4547:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000080 \