 erythrocyte clearance. Markers include F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68-positive, sialoadhesin-positive, CD163/SRCR-positive. Irregular, with long processes including lamellipodia extending into the sinusoid lumen, have flattened nucleus with cytoplasm containing characteristic invaginations of the plasma membrane (vermiform bodies); lie within the sinusoid lumen attached to the endothelial surface; derived from the bone marrow, form a major part of the body's mononuclear phagocyte system.\")\n4647:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000091 \"BTO:0000685\")\n4648:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000091 \"FMA:14656\")\n4649:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"hepatic macrophage\")\n4650:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"littoral cell of hepatic sinusoid\")\n4651:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"liver macrophage\")\n4652:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"macrophagocytus stellatus\")\n4653:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"stellate cell of von Kupffer\")\n4654:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000091 \"von Kupffer cell\")\n4655:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000091 \"Markers: Mouse: F4/80+, CD11b-low, CD68+, sialoadhesin+, CD163/SRCR+; role or process: immune, antigen-presentation, clearance of senescent erythrocytes, iron metabolism. Kupffer cells are also reportedly C3aR-positive, CD14-low, CD54-positive, CD88-positive, and CD284-positive. They are also capable of producing IL-1, IL-6, TNF-alpha, nitric oxide, PGD2, PGE2, PGF2alpha, and TXA2.\")\n4656:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000091 \"Kupffer cell\")\n4657:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000091 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000864 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0001025 obo:UBERON_0001281) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001813) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000001925) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000002064) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0034102) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0015016 obo:PR_000001012)))\n4658:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000091 obo:CL_0000864)\n4660:# Class: obo:CL_0000092 (osteoclast)\n4662:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10428500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15055519\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17380158\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000092 \"A specialized phagocytic cell associated with the absorption and removal of the mineralized matrix of bone tissue, which typically differentiates from monocytes. This cell has the following markers: tartrate-resistant acid phosphatase type 5-positive, PU.1-positive, c-fos-positive, nuclear factor NF-kappa-B p100 subunit-positive, tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 11A-positive and macrophage colony-stimulating factor 1 receptor-positive.\")\n4663:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"BTO:0000968\")\n4664:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"CALOHA:TS-0721\")\n4665:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"FMA:66781\")\n4666:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000092 \"MESH:D010010\")\n4667:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000092 \"chondroclast\")\n4668:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000092 \"Morphology: Highly vesicular; markers: Surface: RANK, cFMS (MCSF receptor); Secreted: cathepsin K and TRAP (tartate resistant acid phosphatase); transcription factors: PU.1, cFOS, MITF, NFkB (p52); role or process: tissue remodelling: bone resorption; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n4669:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000092 \"osteoclast\")\n4670:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000092 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000766 Object