pedia says that cementocytes no longer produce cementum, but the phenoscape def is: Skeletogenic cell that produces cementum, is part of the odontogenic papilla, and is a transformation of a cementoblast cell (no change to existing def).\")\n5189:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000141 \"cementocyte\")\n5190:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000141 obo:CL_0000137)\n5191:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000141 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0005176))\n5192:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000141 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000061))\n5194:# Class: obo:CL_0000142 (hyalocyte)\n5196:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19073178\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000142 \"A cell occurring in the peripheral part of the vitreous body of the eye that may be responsible for production of hyaluronic acid and collagen.\")\n5197:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000142 \"BTO:0004271\")\n5198:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000142 \"FMA:70620\")\n5199:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000142 \"vitreous cell\")\n5200:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000142 \"hyalocyte\")\n5201:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000142 obo:CL_0000499)\n5203:# Class: obo:CL_0000143 (guidepost cell)\n5205:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000143 \"guidepost cell\")\n5206:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000143 obo:CL_0000130)\n5208:# Class: obo:CL_0000144 (obsolete cell by function)\n5210:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"FB:ma\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000144 \"OBSOLETE: A classification of cells by their primary end goal or behavior.\")\n5211:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0000000\")\n5212:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0000003\")\n5213:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000144 \"CL:0001034\")\n5214:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000144 \"This term was made obsolete because there is no difference in meaning between it and 'cell', as any cell can be classified by its function or behavior. If you have used this term in annotation, please replace it with cell (CL:0000000), native cell (CL:0000003), or cell in vitro (CL:0001034) as appropriate.\")\n5215:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000144 \"obsolete cell by function\")\n5216:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000144 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n5218:# Class: obo:CL_0000145 (professional antigen presenting cell)\n5220:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000145 \"A cell capable of processing and presenting lipid and protein antigens to T cells in order to initiate an immune response.\")\n5221:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000145 \"APC\")\n5222:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000145 \"Note change of name; nearly all somatic cells can present antigens to T cells via MHC Class I complexes leading to effector responses, but professional antigen presenting cells constitutively express MHC Class II as well as costimulatory molecules, and thus can initiate immune responses via T cells.\")\n5223:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000145 \"professional antigen presenting cell\")\n5224:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000145 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000738 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002504)))\n5225:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000145 obo:CL_0000738)\n5227:# Class: obo:CL_0000146 (simple columnar epithelial cell)\n5229:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000146 \"simple columnar epithelial cell\")\n5230:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000146 obo:CL_0000075)\n5232:# Class: obo:CL_0000147 (pigment cell)\n5234:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000147 \"A pigment cell is a cell that contains pigment granules.\")\n5235:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000147 \"VHOG:0001678\")\n5236:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000147 \"chromatocyte\")\n5237:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000147 \"chromatophore\")\n5238:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000147 \"pigment cell\")\n5239:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000147 obo:CL_0000325)\n5241:# Class: obo:CL_0000148 (melanocyte)\n5243:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000148 \"A pigment cell derived from the neural crest. Contains melanin-filled pigment granules, which gives a brown to black appearance.\")\n5244:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"BTO:0000847\")\n5245:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"CALOHA:TS-0613\")\n5246:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"FMA:70545\")\n5247:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"MESH:D008544\")\n5248:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000148 \"VHOG:0001679\")\n5249:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000148 \"melanophore\")\n5250:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000148 \"melanocyte\")\n5251:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000148 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000147 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0042470) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000541)))\n5253:# Class: obo:CL_0000149 (visual pigment cell)\n5255:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000149 \"pigment cell\")\n5256:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000149 \"visual pigment cell\")\n5257:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000149 obo:CL_0000147)\n5259:# Class: obo:CL_0000150 (glandular secretory epithelial cell)\n5261:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ORCID:0000-0002-7073-9172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000150 \"An epithelial cell, located in a gland, that is specialised for the synthesis and secretion of specific biomolecules, such as hormones, or mucous.\")\n5262:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000150 \"CALOHA:TS-2085\")\n5263:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000150 \"FMA:86494\")\n5264:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000150 \"glandular epithelial cell\")\n5265:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000150 \"glandular secretory epithelial cell\")\n5266:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000150 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002530)))\n5268:# Class: obo:CL_0000151 (secretory cell)\n5270:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000151 \"A cell that specializes in controlled release of one or more substances.\")\n5271:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000151 \"BTO:0003659\")\n5272:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000151 \"FMA:86916\")\n5273:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000151 \"secretory cell\")\n5274:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032940)))\n5276:# Class: obo:CL_0000152 (exocrine cell)\n5278:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0198547684\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000152 \"A cell of an exocrine gland; i.e. a gland that discharges its secretion via a duct.\")\n5279:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000152 \"FMA:16014\")\n5280:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000152 \"exocrine cell\")\n5281:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000152 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002365)))\n5282:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000152 obo:CL_0000151)\n5284:# Class: obo:CL_0000153 (glycosaminoglycan secreting cell)\n5286:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000153 \"A cell that secretes glycosaminoglycans.\")\n5287:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000153 \"GAG secreting cell\")\n5288:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_0000153 \"hyaluronic acid secreting cell\")\n5289:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000153 \"glycosaminoglycan secreting cell\")\n5290:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000153 obo:CL_0000327)\n5291:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000153 obo:CL_0000447)\n5293:# Class: obo:CL_0000154 (protein secreting cell)\n5295:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000154 \"protein secreting cell\")\n5296:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000154 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0009306)))\n5298:# Class: obo:CL_0000155 (peptic cell)\n5300:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21907708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30571046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Gastric_chief_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000155 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by a basally located nucleus, abundant rough endoplasmic reticulum, and large apical secretory granules. It produces and secretes pepsinogen, the inactive precursor of the digestive enzyme pepsin.\")\n5301:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000155 \"FMA:62902\")\n5302:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"chief cell of stomach\")\n5303:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Chief_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"gastric chief cell\")\n5304:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"pepsinogen secreting cell\")\n5305:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Chief_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000155 \"zymogenic cell\")\n5306:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000155 \"peptic cell\")\n5307:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 obo:CL_0000154)\n5308:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 obo:CL_0002178)\n5309:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001276))\n5310:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000155 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010038))\n5312:# Class: obo:CL_0000156 (obsolete antibody secreting cell)\n5314:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000156 \"OBSOLETE: A cell of the lymphoid series that can react with antigen to produce specific cell products called antibodies. Various cell subpopulations, often B cells, can be defined, based on the different classes of immunoglobulins that they synthesize.\")\n5315:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000156 \"Consider using 'B cell ; CL:0000236' or one of its children instead.\")\n5316:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000156 \"obsolete antibody secreting cell\")\n5317:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000156 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n5319:# Class: obo:CL_0000157 (surfactant secreting cell)\n5321:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000157 \"A cell that specializes in secretion of surfactant in the alveoli of the lung.\")\n5322:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000157 \"surfactant secreting cell\")\n5323:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000157 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000151 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0043129)))\n5324:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000157 obo:CL_0000151)\n5326:# Class: obo:CL_0000158 (club cell)\n5328:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1183/09031936.00146609\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1378/chest.12-2762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28128362\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29874100\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7905712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000158 \"A non-mucous, epithelial secretory cell that is part of the tracheobronchial tree. A club cell has short microvilli but no cilia. A club cell is able to multiply and differentiate into ciliated cells to regenerate the bronchiolar epithelium and it also protects the tracheobronchial epithelium.\")\n5329:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000158 \"BTO:0004811\")\n5330:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000158 \"FMA:14119\")\n5331:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000158 \"Clara cell\")\n5332:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000158 \"club cell\")\n5333:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000158 obo:CL_0002202)\n5334:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000158 obo:CL_0011026)\n5335:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000158 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:GO_0005902))\n5336:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000158 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0032940))\n5337:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000158 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0043129))\n5339:# Class: obo:CL_0000159 (seromucus secreting cell)\n5341:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000159 \"seromucus secreting cell\")\n5342:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000159 obo:CL_0000151)\n5344:# Class: obo:CL_0000160 (goblet cell)\n5346:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D020397\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000160 \"A specialized, columnar, mucus secreting epithelial cell shaped like a flask or goblet. A narrow basal end contains the nucleus while the apical end is swollen by the accumulation of mucus laden secretory granules.  Short microvilli project from the apical plasma membrane.\")\n5347:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"BTO:0001540\")\n5348:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"FMA:13148\")\n5349:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000160 \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goblet_cell\")\n5350:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000160 \"chalice cell\")\n5351:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000160 \"goblet cell\")\n5352:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <http://cnx.org/content/col11496/1.6/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=30131227>) foaf:depiction obo:CL_0000160 \"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg/800px-404_Goblet_Cell_new.jpg\")\n5353:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000160 obo:CL_0000066)\n5354:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005902))\n5355:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0098594))\n5356:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070254))\n5358:# Class: obo:CL_0000161 (obsolete acid secreting cell)\n5360:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000161 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/427>)\n5361:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:consider obo:CL_0000161 obo:CL_0000162)\n5362:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000161 \"obsolete acid secreting cell\")\n5363:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000161 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n5365:# Class: obo:CL_0000162 (parietal cell)\n5367:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31670611\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000162 \"An epithelial cell of the stomach that is part of the fundic gastric gland. This cell is characterized by its pyramidal shape, abundant mitochondria, and a complex network of secretory canaliculi lined with microvilli. It secretes hydrochloric acid into the stomach lumen and produces intrinsic factor, essential for vitamin B12 absorption.\")\n5368:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000162 \"BTO:0001780\")\n5369:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000162 \"FMA:62901\")\n5370:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29263912\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000162 \"gastric parietal cell\")\n5371:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Parietal_cell\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000162 \"oxyntic cell\")\n5372:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29263912\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613538\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000162 \"Parietal cells have dynamic, actin-supported microvilli that increase in number during active secretion, playing a crucial role in secreting hydrochloric acid and intrinsic factor. The structure and regulation of these microvilli are influenced by proteins such as ASAP3, which modulates Arf6 activity and actin assembly, thereby controlling microvilli formation and parietal cell function.\")\n5373:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000162 \"parietal cell\")\n5374:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 obo:CL_0000151)\n5375:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 obo:CL_0002178)\n5376:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001276))\n5377:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010038))\n5378:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005902))\n5379:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001696))\n5381:# Class: obo:CL_0000163 (endocrine cell)\n5383:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055098\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000163 \"A cell of an endocrine gland, ductless glands that secrete substances which are released directly into the circulation and which influence metabolism and other body functions.\")\n5384:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000163 \"FMA:83809\")\n5385:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000163 \"endocrinocyte\")\n5386:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000163 \"endocrine cell\")\n5387:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000163 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0046879 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002339 obo:UBERON_0001009)))))\n5388:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000163 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000949))\n5390:# Class: obo:CL_0000164 (enteroendocrine cell)\n5392:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"SANBI:mhl\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000164 \"An endocrine cell that is located in the epithelium of the gastrointestinal tract or in the pancreas.\")\n5393:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"BTO:0003865\")\n5394:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"FMA:62930\")\n5395:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000164 \"MESH:D019858\")\n5396:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000164 \"enteroendocrine cell\")\n5397:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000164 obo:CL_0000066)\n5398:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000164 obo:CL_0000163)\n5400:# Class: obo:CL_0000165 (neuroendocrine cell)\n5402:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D055099\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000165 \"A neuron that is capable of some hormone secretion in response to neuronal signals.\")\n5403:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000165 \"BTO:0002691\")\n5404:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000165 \"FMA:83810\")\n5405:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000165 \"neurosecretory cell\")\n5406:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000165 \"neurosecretory neuron\")\n5407:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:5342440\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.clinicalkey.com/#!/content/book/3-s2.0-B9780323555968000073\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000165 \"The neurosecretory cell is neither an ordinary neuron nor an endocrine cell, but a combination of both. Its neuronal features resemble those of ordinary neurons concerning both structure and function. The production of a visible secretory material marks the neurosecretory neuron as a gland cell, and the fact that extractable cellular products act in the manner of hormones places it in the realm of endocrine elements. \n5410:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000165 \"neuroendocrine cell\")\n5411:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000165 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046879)))\n5412:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000165 obo:CL_0000163)\n5413:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000165 obo:CL_0000393)\n54