42-positive, CD61-positive, CD62P-positive, CD64-positive, CD89-positive, CD102-positive, CD147-positive (activated platelets), CD154-positive (activated platelets), CD162-positive, CD209, CD282-positive, CD284-positive, CD289-positive, CD181-negative, CD182-negative, CD183-negative, CD184-positive, CLEC2-positive, GPVI-positive, JAMC-positive, PAR1-positive, PAR2-negative, PAR3-positive, PAR4-positive, TSP1-positive, and TXA2R-positive. Platelets can reportedly produce CCL2, CCL3, CCL5, CCL7, CCL17, CD40L, CXCL1, CXCL4, CXCL4L1, CXCL5, CXCL7, CXCL8, CXCL12, EGF, factor V, factor VII, factor XI, factor XIII, bFGF, histamine, IGF-1, IL-1beta, PAI-1, PDGF, plasminogen, protein S, serotonin, TGF-beta, TFPI, VEGF, and vWF.\")\n6009:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000233 \"platelet\")\n6010:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 obo:CL_0000081)\n6011:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000233 obo:CL_0000763)\n6012:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001405))\n6013:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0001874))\n6014:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000556))\n6015:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001820))\n6016:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000233 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002216 obo:GO_0007596))\n6018:# Class: obo:CL_0000234 (phagocyte)\n6020:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000234 \"Any cell capable of ingesting particulate matter via phagocytosis.\")\n6021:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000234 \"BTO:0001044\")\n6022:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000234 \"FMA:83806\")\n6023:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000234 \"MESH:D010586\")\n6024:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000234 \"phagocyte\")\n6025:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000234 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909)))\n6026:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000234 obo:CL_0000219)\n6027:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000234 obo:CL_0000325)\n6029:# Class: obo:CL_0000235 (macrophage)\n6031:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16213494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1919437\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000235 \"A mononuclear phagocyte present in variety of tissues, typically differentiated from monocytes, capable of phagocytosing a variety of extracellular particulate material, including immune complexes, microorganisms, and dead cells.\")\n6032:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000235 \"BTO:0000801\")\n6033:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000235 \"CALOHA:TS-0587\")\n6034:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000235 \"FMA:63261\")\n6035:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000235 \"FMA:83585\")\n6036:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000235 \"MESH:D008264\")\n6037:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000235 \"histiocyte\")\n6038:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000235 \"Morphology: Diameter 30_M-80 _M, abundant cytoplasm, low N/C ratio, eccentric nucleus. Irregular shape with pseudopods, highly adhesive. Contain vacuoles and phagosomes, may contain azurophilic granules; markers: Mouse & Human: CD68, in most cases CD11b. Mouse: in most cases F4/80+; role or process: immune, antigen presentation, & tissue remodelling; lineage: hematopoietic, myeloid.\")\n6039:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000235 \"macrophage\")\n6040:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000235 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000766 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0002504) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0031268)))\n6041:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000235 obo:CL_0000113)\n6042:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000235 obo:CL_0000766)\n6043:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000235 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000576))\n6045:# Class: obo:CL_0000236 (B cell)\n6047:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000236 \"A lymphocyte of B lineage that is capable of B cell mediated immunity.\")\n6048:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000236 \"BTO:0000776\")\n6049:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000236 \"CALOHA:TS-0068\")\n6050:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000236 \"FMA:62869\")\n6051:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000236 \"MESH:D001402\")\n6052:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000236 \"VHOG:0001480\")\n6053:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000236 \"B lymphocyte\")\n6054:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000236 \"B-cell\")\n6055:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000236 \"B-lymphocyte\")\n6056:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000236 \"B cell\")\n6057:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000236 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000945 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0019724)))\n6058:SubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:is_inferred \"true\") obo:CL_0000236 obo:CL_0000945)\n6059:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000236 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000826))\n6061:# Class: obo:CL_0000237 (keratinizing barrier epithelial cell)\n6063:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000237 \"keratinizing barrier epithelial cell\")\n6064:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000237 obo:CL_0000240)\n6065:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000237 obo:CL_0000311)\n6066:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000237 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000114))\n6068:# Class: obo:CL_0000238 (non keratinizing barrier epithelial cell)\n6070:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000238 \"non keratinizing barrier epithelial cell\")\n6071:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000238 obo:CL_0000240)\n6073:# Class: obo:CL_0000239 (brush border epithelial cell)\n6075:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000239 \"An epithelial cell characterized by the presence of a brush border on its apical surface, which increases the surface area for absorption.\")\n6076:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 <https://doi.org/10.1152/ajpgi.00005.2011>)\n6077:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000239 \"PMID:25422372\")\n6078:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000239 \"All brush border cells are columnar-cuboidal.  The formal logical definition of this term asserts this. Brush border epithelial cells are predominantly found lining the small intestine and the proximal tubules of the kidneys.\")\n6079:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000239 \"brush border epithelial cell\")\n6080:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000239 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0005903)))\n6081:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000239 obo:CL_0000075)\n6083:# Class: obo:CL_0000240 (stratified squamous epithelial cell)\n6085:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Epithelium\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_squamous_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000240 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of squamous epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cells. The basal layer is directly attached to the basement membrane and the apical layer consists of flattened squamous cells. This provides a protective barrier, commonly found in areas subject to abrasion, such as the skin, oral cavity, and esophagus.\")\n6086:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000240 \"stratified squamous epithelial cell\")\n6087:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000240 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0006915)))\n6088:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000240 obo:CL_0000076)\n6090:# Class: obo:CL_0000241 (stratified cuboidal epithelial cell)\n6092:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30422572\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Stratified_cuboidal_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000241 \"A stratified epithelial cell that is part of cuboidal epithelium, characterized by multiple layers of cuboidal cells forming the apical layer. This provides a protective lining for ducts in large glands, such as sweat glands.\")\n6093:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000241 \"stratified cuboidal epithelial cell\")\n6094:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000241 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000079 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0010077)))\n6095:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000241 obo:CL_0000075)\n6097:# Class: obo:CL_0000242 (Merkel cell)\n6099:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D018862\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19834574\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2274847\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24862916\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30415995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Merkel_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000242 \"A specialized epithelial cell located in the skin epidermis and certain mucosal epithelia. It functions as a mechanoreceptor for light touch by forming synapse-like contacts with somatosensory afferent nerve endings, contributing to slowly adapting type I (SAI) tactile responses. Characterized by dense-core neuroendocrine granules, the Merkel cell exhibits both sensory and neuroendocrine properties, including regulated neurotransmitter release via SNARE complex-dependent mechanisms. Its development in mice depends on the transcription factor Atoh1.\")\n6100:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_0000242 \"FMA:70548\")\n6101:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000242 \"Merkel's cell\")\n6102:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24862916\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000242 \"MC\")\n6103:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000242 \"Merkel cell\")\n6104:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000242 obo:CL_0000066)\n6105:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000242 obo:CL_0000123)\n6106:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000242 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0031201))\n6107:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000242 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0007269))\n6109:# Class: obo:CL_0000243 (obsolete glial cell (sensu Vertebrata))\n6111:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"MESH:D009457\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000243 \"A non-neuronal cell of the nervous system. They not only provide physical support, but also respond to injury, regulate the ionic and chemical composition of the extracellular milieu. Form the myelin insulation of nervous pathways, guide neuronal migration during development, and exchange metabolites with neurons. Neuroglia have high-affinity transmitter uptake systems, voltage-dependent and transmitter-gated ion channels, and can release transmitters, but their role in signaling (as in many other functions) is unclear.\")\n6112:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000233 obo:CL_0000243 <https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/715>)\n6113:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000243 \"This is a grouping class that is no longer needed or wanted.\")\n6114:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000243 \"obsolete glial cell (sensu Vertebrata)\")\n6115:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000243 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6117:# Class: obo:CL_0000244 (transitional epithelial cell)\n6119:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000244 \"A cell characteristically found lining hollow organs that are subject to great mechanical change due to contraction and distention; originally thought to represent a transition between stratified squamous and columnar epithelium.\")\n6120:AnnotationAssertion(o