 morphologically distinguishable from the epidermal cells composing the groundmass of the tissue.\")\n6296:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000270 obo:PO_0000284)\n6297:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000270 \"obsolete subsidiary cell\")\n6298:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000270 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6300:# Class: obo:CL_0000271 (obsolete prestalk A cell)\n6302:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000271 obo:DDANAT_0000408)\n6303:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000271 \"obsolete prestalk A cell\")\n6304:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000271 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6306:# Class: obo:CL_0000272 (obsolete cambial initial)\n6308:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000272 \"OBSOLETE, use term from Plant Ontology. A cell localized in the vascular cambium or phellogen. Its periclinal division can contribute cells either to the outside or to the inside of the axis; in vascular cambium, classified into fusiform initials (source of axial cells of xylem and phloem) and ray initials (source of the ray cells).\")\n6309:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000272 \"replaced_by PO:0000295\")\n6310:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000272 \"obsolete cambial initial\")\n6311:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000272 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6313:# Class: obo:CL_0000273 (obsolete prestalk AB cell)\n6315:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000273 obo:DDANAT_0000410)\n6316:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000273 \"obsolete prestalk AB cell\")\n6317:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000273 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6319:# Class: obo:CL_0000274 (obo:CL_0000274)\n6321:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000231 obo:CL_0000274 obo:IAO_0000227)\n6322:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000274 obo:CL_0000009)\n6323:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000274 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6325:# Class: obo:CL_0000275 (obsolete prestalk B cell)\n6327:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000275 obo:DDANAT_0000409)\n6328:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000275 \"obsolete prestalk B cell\")\n6329:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000275 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6331:# Class: obo:CL_0000276 (obsolete sclerenchyma cell)\n6333:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000276 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000077 from Plant Ontology instead. Cell variable in form and size, being more or less thick, often lignified, secondary walls. Belongs to the category of subcells and may or may not be devoid of protoplast at maturity.\")\n6334:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000276 obo:PO_0000077)\n6335:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000276 \"obsolete sclerenchyma cell\")\n6336:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000276 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6338:# Class: obo:CL_0000277 (obsolete prestalk I cell)\n6340:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DictyBase:DDB\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000277 \"OBSOLETE: Initial population of prestalk cells that activate the ecmA promoter at the mound stage and that presumably further differentiate into pstA and pstO cells.\")\n6341:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000277 obo:DDANAT_0000406)\n6342:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000277 \"This cell type does not exist in Dictyostelium. it has been long deleted in their anatomy ontology.\")\n6343:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000277 \"obsolete prestalk I cell\")\n6344:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000277 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6346:# Class: obo:CL_0000278 (obsolete central cell)\n6348:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"TAIR:lr\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000278 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0020090 from Plant Ontology instead. OBSOLETED, use term from Plant Ontology. A cell containing the two polar nuclei which, after double fertilization, will develop into the endosperm.\")\n6349:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000278 obo:PO_0020090)\n6350:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000278 \"obsolete central cell\")\n6351:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000278 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6353:# Class: obo:CL_0000279 (obsolete prestalk 0 cell)\n6355:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000279 obo:DDANAT_0000407)\n6356:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000279 \"obsolete prestalk 0 cell\")\n6357:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000279 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6359:# Class: obo:CL_0000280 (obsolete generative cell)\n6361:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"TAIR:lr\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000280 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0020097 from Plant Ontology instead. The cell that will give rise to the generative nuclei which will participate in fertilization.\")\n6362:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000280 obo:PO_0020097)\n6363:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000280 \"obsolete generative cell\")\n6364:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000280 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6366:# Class: obo:CL_0000281 (obsolete pstAB/ALC)\n6368:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000281 obo:DDANAT_0000411)\n6369:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000281 \"obsolete pstAB/ALC\")\n6370:AnnotationAssertion(owl:deprecated obo:CL_0000281 \"true\"^^xsd:boolean)\n6372:# Class: obo:CL_0000282 (obsolete trichome)\n6374:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0471245208\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10938806\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000282 \"Obsolete. Use PO:0000282 from Plant Ontology instead. An outgrowth from the epidermis. Trichomes vary in size and complexity and include hairs, scales, and other structures and may be glandular. In Arabidopsis, patterning of trichome development is not random but does not appear to be lineage-based like stomata.\")\n6375:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0100001 obo:CL_0000282 obo:PO_0000282)\n6376:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000282 \"obsolete tri