dermal papilla located at the bottom of hair follicles. This cell orchestrates reciprocal epithelial-mesenchymal signaling essential for hair follicle morphogenesis and cycling, regulating matrix cell proliferation and differentiation to control hair shaft size, shape, and growth. The dermal papilla cell is replenished each hair cycle from bipotent hair follicle dermal stem cells in the dermal sheath that simultaneously self-renew and contribute progeny to the papilla, particularly during anagen.\")\n6844:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39798934\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000346 \"hair follicle DPC\")\n6845:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21444748\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_0000346 \"The dermal papilla contains functionally heterogeneous Sox2-positive subpopulations that serve as a niche for multipotent stem cells. These cells exhibit progenitor properties, generate skin-derived precursors (SKPs), and can differentiate into adipogenic and osteogenic lineages.\")\n6846:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000346 \"hair follicle dermal papilla cell\")\n6847:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000346 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000057 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000412)))\n6848:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000346 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0042634))\n6849:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000346 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0060638))\n6850:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000346 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002596 obo:GO_0031069))\n6852:# Class: obo:CL_0000347 (scleral cell)\n6854:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000347 \"A cell of the sclera of the eye.\")\n6855:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000347 \"scleral cell\")\n6856:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0000347 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001773)))\n6857:SubClassOf(obo:CL_0000347 ObjectSomeValue