interneuron)\n31216:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25303526\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023122 \"An interneuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses the oxytocin receptor. These interneurons also express somatostatin.\")\n31217:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25303526\") obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_4023122 obo:NCBITaxon_10090)\n31218:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023122 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31219:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25303526\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023122 \"OxtrINs\")\n31220:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25303526\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023122 \"These cells were first identified in mouse.\")\n31221:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023122 \"oxytocin receptor sst GABAergic cortical interneuron\")\n31222:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 obo:CL_0000099)\n31223:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956))\n31224:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n31225:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001635))\n31226:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023122 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\n31228:# Class: obo:CL_4023123 (hypothalamus kisspeptin neuron)\n31230:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30042117\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023123 \"A kisspeptin neuron that is located in the hypothalamus. These neurons project to and activate gonadotrophin-releasing hormone neurons (acting via the kisspeptin receptor) in the hypothalamus and stimulate the secretion of gonadotrophin-releasing hormone.\")\n31231:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023123 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31232:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023123 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31233:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023123 \"hypothalamus kisspeptin neuron\")\n31234:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023123 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023130 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001898)))\n31236:# Class: obo:CL_4023124 (dentate gyrus kisspeptin neuron)\n31238:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Kisspeptin&oldid=1042853037\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023124 \"A kisspeptin neuron that is located in the dentate gyrus of the hippocampus.\")\n31239:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023124 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31240:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023124 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31241:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023124 \"dentate gyrus kisspeptin neuron\")\n31242:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023124 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023130 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001885)))\n31244:# Class: obo:CL_4023125 (KNDy neuron)\n31246:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:KNDy_neuron&oldid=964682278\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023125 \"A hypothalamus kisspeptin neuron that coexpresses kisspeptin, neurokinin B and dynorphin.\")\n31247:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023125 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31248:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023125 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31249:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023125 \"kisspeptin, neurokinin B and dynorphin expressing neuron\")\n31250:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:KNDy_neuron&oldid=964682278\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023125 \"KNDy neurons are involved in the negative feedback of gonadotropin-releasing hormone release in the hypothalamic–pituitary–gonadal axis. Sex steroids released from the gonads act on KNDy neurons as inhibitors of kisspeptin release. This inhibition provides negative feedback control on the hypothalamic–pituitary–gonadal axis. Other roles of KNDy neurons include influences on prolactin production; puberty; stress' effects on reproduction; and the control of thermoregulation.\")\n31251:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023125 \"KNDy neuron\")\n31252:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023125 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023123 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000012526) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000016004)))\n31254:# Class: obo:CL_4023127 (arcuate nucleus of hypothalamus KNDy neuron)\n31256:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30042117\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023127 \"a KNDy neuron that is located in the arcuate nucleus of the hypothalamus.\")\n31257:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023127 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31258:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023127 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31259:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023127 \"arcuate nucleus of hypothalamus KNDy neuron\")\n31260:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023127 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023125 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001932)))\n31262:# Class: obo:CL_4023128 (rostral periventricular region of the third ventricle KNDy neuron)\n31264:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30042117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:KNDy_neuron&oldid=964682278\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023128 \"a KNDy neuron that is located in the rostral periventricular region of the third ventricle.\")\n31265:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Anteroventral_periventricular_nucleus&oldid=966137187\") obo:IAO_0000116 obo:CL_4023128 \"In rats and mice, the anteroventral periventricular nucleus plus the periventricular nucleus make up the rostral periventricular region of the third ventricle (RP3V).\")\n31266:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023128 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31267:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023128 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31268:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023128 \"RP3V KNDy neuron\")\n31269:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023128 \"rostral periventricular region of the third ventricle KNDy neuron\")\n31270:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023128 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023125 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_8440005)))\n31272:# Class: obo:CL_4023129 (retinoblast)\n31274:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17565741\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023129 \"A retinal cell that is immature or undifferentiated.\")\n31275:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023129 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31276:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023129 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31277:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17565741\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023129 \"retinal stem cell\")\n31278:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023129 \"retinoblast\")\n31279:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023129 obo:CL_0009004)\n31280:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023129 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000966))\n31282:# Class: obo:CL_4023130 (kisspeptin neuron)\n31284:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30042117\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023130 \"A neuron that expresses kisspeptin. These neurons are predominantly located in the hypothalamus, but also found in other parts of the brain including the hippocampal dentate gyrus.\")\n31285:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023130 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31286:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023130 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473>)\n31287:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30042117\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023130 \"Gonadal sex steroids stimulate kisspeptin neurons in the RP3V, but inhibit kisspeptin neurons in the ARC.\")\n31288:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023130 \"kisspeptin neuron\")\n31289:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023130 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000009344)))\n31290:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023130 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001017))\n31292:# Class: obo:CL_4023154 (myelinating glial cell)\n31294:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.1007/3-540-29623-9_3240\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023154 \"A glial cell that myelinates axonal processes.\")\n31295:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023154 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31296:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023154 \"myelinating glial cell\")\n31297:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023154 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000125 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0043209)))\n31299:# Class: obo:CL_4023158 (octopus cell of the mammalian cochlear nucleus)\n31301:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:title=Cochlear_nucleus&oldid=1090176664\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023158 \"A neuron in the posterior ventral cochlear nucleus that is distinguished by their long, thick and tentacle-shaped dendrites that typically emanate from one side of the cell body.\")\n31302:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000116 obo:CL_4023158 \"This term is restricted to the mammalian cochlear nucleus to disambiguate for cells of octopus.\")\n31303:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023158 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31304:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11976365\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:title=Cochlear_nucleus&oldid=1090176664\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023158 \"Octopus cells respond only at the onset of a broad-band simple tonal stimulus and form a pathway to the superior paraolivary nucleus and to the ventral nucleus of the lateral lemniscus.\")\n31305:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023158 \"octopus cell of the mammalian cochlear nucleus\")\n31306:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023158 obo:CL_0000540)\n31307:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023158 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002831))\n31308:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023158 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0013001 obo:UBERON_8440043))\n31310:# Class: obo:CL_4023159 (double bouquet cell)\n31312:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15378039\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023159 \"An interneuron that has double bouquet morphology.\")\n31313:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023159 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31314:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023159 \"double bouquet cell\")\n31315:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023159 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070061)))\n31317:# Class: obo:CL_4023160 (cartwheel cell)\n31319:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ILX:0102311\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Cartwheel_cell&oldid=1040398094\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023160 \"A neuron of the dorsal cochlear nucleus with spiny dendrites that receive input from the axons of granule cells and with axons that release GABA and glycine onto cartwheel, pyramidal and giant cell targets.\")\n31320:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023160 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31321:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4023160 \"ILX:0102311\")\n31322:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ILX:0102311\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023160 \"Cartwheel cells share many of the features, molecular and electrophysiological, of cerebellar Purkinje neurons.\")\n31323:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023160 \"cartwheel cell\")\n31324:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023160 obo:CL_0000540)\n31325:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002829))\n31326:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002103 obo:CL_0000120))\n31327:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\n31328:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023160 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537))\n31330:# Class: obo:CL_4023161 (unipolar brush cell)\n31332:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9193142\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Unipolar_brush_cell&oldid=1045937026\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023161 \"An excitatory glutamatergic interneuron found in the granular layer of the cerebellar cortex and also in the granule cell domain of the cochlear nucleus. Unipolar brush cells have a round or oval cell body with usually a single short dendrite that ends in a brush-like tuft of short dendrites unique to them known as dendrioles.\")\n31333:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023161 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31334:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4023161 \"neuronal brush cell\")\n31335:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023161 \"unipolar brush cell\")\n31336:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1016/j.cnp.2022.11.002\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4023161 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/CB_circuits_PMID3650468_f2.png>)\n31337:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fnins.2020.00293\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4023161 <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Candelabrum_cell.jpg>)\n31338:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023161 obo:CL_0000099)\n31339:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0044293))\n31340:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070025))\n31341:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002028))\n31342:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023161 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061535))\n31344:# Class: obo:CL_4023162 (bushy cell)\n31346:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Bushy_cell&oldid=879061753\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023162 \"A neuron found in the anterior part of the ventral cochlear nucleus that has the appearance of bushes, having short dendrites. Bushy cells give outputs to different parts of the superior olivary complex.\")\n31347:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023162 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31348:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023162 \"bushy cell\")\n31349:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023162 obo:CL_0000540)\n31350:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0002830))\n31351:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023162 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0013001 obo:UBERON_0002128))\n31353:# Class: obo:CL_4023163 (spherical bushy cell)\n31355:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31881018\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Bushy_cell&oldid=879061753\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023163 \"A bushy cell that receives only few large excitatory endbulb synapses from auditory nerves. Spherical bush cells give excitatory input to the lateral and medial parts of the superior olive.\")\n31356:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023163 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31357:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31881018\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023163 \"SBC\")\n31358:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023163 \"spherical bushy cell\")\n31359:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023163 obo:CL_4023162)\n31361:# Class: obo:CL_4023164 (globular bushy cell)\n31363:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31881018\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Bushy_cell&oldid=879061753\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023164 \"A bushy cell that receives a large number of medium-sized synapses, called modified endbulbs. Globular bushy cells extend to the superior olive on both sides of the brainstem where they give input to the bipolar neurons.\")\n31364:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023164 <http://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\n31365:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboI