 \"There are midget bipolar cells of retina and midget ganglion cells of retina and they are not the same:\n31425:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023188 \"midget ganglion cell of retina\")\n31426:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023188 obo:CL_0000740)\n31427:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023188 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0013001 obo:UBERON_0013607))\n31429:# Class: obo:CL_4023189 (parasol ganglion cell of retina)\n31431:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32533915\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Parasol_cell&oldid=1032171532\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023189 \"A retinal ganglion cell located in the ganglion cell layer of the retina. This cell projects to magnocellular cells in the lateral geniculate nucleus (LGN). They have large cell bodies and extensive, branching dendritic networks that contribute to their large receptive fields.\")\n31432:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023189 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596\")\n31433:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023189 \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\")\n31434:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023189 \"M cell\")\n31435:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4023189 \"M ganglion cell\")\n31436:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_4023189 \"These cells should not be confused with M1-M14 retinal ganglion cells described in PMID:16626866 which refer to a different classification of retinal ganglion cells.\")\n31437:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023189 \"parasol ganglion cell of retina\")\n31438:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023189 obo:CL_0000740)\n31439:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4023189 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0013001 obo:UBERON_0013606))\n31441:# Class: obo:CL_4028001 (pulmonary capillary endothelial cell)\n31443:AnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4028001 \"Any capillary endothelial cell that is part of a lung.\")\n31444:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4028001 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3293-5463>)\n3144